{title: 350 - Blest Be the Tie That Binds}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #350 • DENNIS • 12.13}
{lyricist: John Fawcett}
{composer: Johann G. Naegeli}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 350}
{meta: tune DENNIS}
{meta: meter 12.13}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Blest be the [C]tie [C7]that [F]binds [Bb]our hearts [F]in Christian [C]love;
[C]The [C7]fellowship [C]of kindred [F]minds is like to [Bb]that [F/C]above.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Before [C7]our [Bb]Father's [C]throne
[F]we pour [C7]our [Bb]ardent [C]prayers;
[C]our [F]fears, our [C]hopes, [Bb/F]our [F]aims are [C7]one,
[C]our [F]comforts [C7]and [Bb/F]our [F]cares.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]We share [C7]each [Bb]other's [C]woes,
[F]our mutual [Bb]burdens [C]bear;
[C]and [F]often [C]for [F]each other flows
[C]the [F]sympathizing tear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]When we [C7]asunder [C]part,
[F]it gives us [Bb]inward [C]pain;
[C]but [F]we shall [C]still [F]be joined [Bb]in [F/C]heart,
[C]and [F]hope [C]to [F]meet again.
{end_of_verse}
